  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we walk into the wood. Woodland birds are often heard before they are seen, and when you do spot one it is usually high up, in a tangle of branches. That is why it helps to know what they do: some climb up the trunk, one climbs down it, and one just flies through with a screech.\n\nA wood is also a good place to practise what you learned in week 4: size and shape first, then colours. We start with the woodpecker, the one everybody wants to see.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of ten questions, with birds from the last two lessons mixed in."
  },
