    "title": {
      "en": "Nuthatch or Treecreeper?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Both climb trunks, but they look different. The Nuthatch is bigger, blue-grey above and orange below, with a black eye stripe, and it climbs down head first. The Treecreeper is small, brown and speckled with a thin curved bill, and it only climbs up."
    }
  },
